From: Nate Chapin <japhet@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:16:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] [M156] Block re-entrant navigations during
 CommitNavigation document abort

Original change's description:
> Block re-entrant navigations during CommitNavigation document abort
>
> FrameLoader::CommitNavigation() calls
> CancelProvisionalLoaderForNewNavigation(), which triggers
> Document::Abort() and can synchronously dispatch a readystatechange
> event. Previously, a listener (or nested run loop such as
> window.print()) could start or commit another navigation
> mid-CommitNavigation(), causing CommitNavigation() to later clone
> ExtraData or overwrite state from an interleaved cross-origin
> DocumentLoader.
>
> Scope a FrameNavigationDisabler around
> CancelProvisionalLoaderForNewNavigation() in CommitNavigation(),
> matching DetachDocument(). Also guard
> ScriptController::ExecuteJavaScriptURL() against running script or
> overwriting the Document if a new Document is committed during the
> Trusted Types pre-navigation check or script execution, even when the
> initial empty LocalDOMWindow is reused.
>
> Fixed: 580879655, 584307204
> Change-Id: Ia47d16f95ff6876f6ba2c836de0deaebfffffa79
